      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "UNCERTAINTY",
      "narration_text": "Instead of a single number, every prediction now comes with a confidence band. Conformal prediction wraps each forecast in a distribution-free interval — seventy-two percent likely to revise, but the true probability sits somewhere between sixty-one and eighty-three. Monte Carlo dropout runs fifty forward passes with dropout active, measuring how much the prediction wobbles. And ensemble disagreement tracks whether all six models agree or scatter. Three lenses on the same question: how sure are we, really?",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "build",
