    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "CONTAGION",
      "narration_text": "Signals don't stay inside one company. When a sector leader starts hedging, peers often follow within one or two quarters. The system now tests for this using Granger causality across every company pair in a sector, building a contagion map of who leads and who lags. It extends to supply chains too — when a supplier's language deteriorates, customers downstream tend to shift one to two quarters later. One company's signal becomes another company's early warning.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
